{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he said to them: Let it be so, YHWH be with you, etc.</b> You say to join YHWH to yourselves when I send you and your little ones, for you are for the service of YHWH and your little ones are for your rejoicing, so that YHWH would be joined with you. Therefore I say, 'Let it be so, YHWH be with you, when I send you and your little ones' — for I have no desire to send the little ones with you, and then YHWH will not be with you either, for it is not fitting to join the name of Heaven with anything else. 'See, for evil is before your faces' (Exodus 10:10) — you are going to slaughter in order to annul the astrological indication of the star whose name is רָעָה, and it is enough for you that you will be saved from the evil; but you seek besides this satiety of joys, to flee from one extreme to the other — this is not a proper thing. 'Not so; go now, the men, and serve YHWH, for that is what you seek' (Exodus 10:11) — that is, the joy — 'that is what you seek': I say that you seek the joy and contrive it from your own hearts, and from the mouth of the Most High it shall not come forth; rather you seek this joy from your own hearts. For you said at first in the name of YHWH, ״וְיָחֹגּוּ לִי בַּמִּדְבָּר״ (Exodus 5:1) — 'to Me' implies for My name alone, to Me and not to yourselves. And how did you say in the name of YHWH, ״כִּי חַג ה׳ לָנוּ״ (Exodus 10:9)? For ״לֹא אִישׁ אֵל וְיִתְנֶחָם״ (Numbers 23:19); rather, surely you seek this from your own hearts. Therefore Pharaoh was filled with wrath against them; consequently ״וַיְגָרֶשׁ אוֹתָם מֵאֵת פְּנֵי פַרְעֹה״ (Exodus 10:11)." "And what is said, ״בִּנְעָרֵינוּ וּבִזְקֵנֵינוּ בְּצֹאנֵנוּ וּבִבְקָרֵנוּ״ (Exodus 10:9), implies that they made themselves subsidiary to all of them, since they did not say 'they shall go with us'; and Pharaoh said, ״גַּם טַפְּכֶם יֵלֵךְ עִמָּכֶם״ (Exodus 10:24), implying that the little ones are subsidiary to them. This will be explained nearby, with the help of YHWH." "<b>See, for evil is before your faces, etc.</b> Because they said, may their memory be for a blessing (Shabbat 156a): 'This one born under the star מַאֲדִים will be a man who sheds blood.' What is his remedy? He should become a slaughterer or a circumciser. And the reason for this is that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not completely overturn the astrological configuration — [He does] only ״this thing that YHWH will do for those who fear Him and for those who think of His name״ (Malachi 3:16): that when the astrological configuration indicates some evil thing, the Holy One, blessed be He, turns the face of the configuration toward another matter similar to it, in such a manner that ״a keeper of the commandment shall know no evil thing״ (Ecclesiastes 8:5), and the judgment of the configuration is maintained in any case." "And in this manner we find (Mo'ed Katan 9a): 'Go to them, that they may bless you.' They said to him, 'May your will be that you sow but do not reap,' etc., 'may your house be destroyed,' etc. He said to them, 'All of these are blessings,' etc. And one asks on this: why did he bless them with parables and riddles? He should have blessed them openly and not with riddles! But because he saw the judgment of the astrological configuration indicating 'you shall sow but not reap,' he wished to turn it into a blessing in such a manner that the judgment of the configuration would be fulfilled and he would not come to harm. So too when Israel went out from Egypt: Pharaoh saw in his astrology that the star מַאֲדִים, whose name is רָעָה, was rising against them, indicating the shedding of blood. And the indication of that star is not corrected except by means of a circumciser (מוֹהֲלָא) or a slaughterer (טַבָּחָא), and both of them together are good — for there is a doubt whether this star indicates actual killing, or only a wound and bruise alone, or both together. Therefore, to correct this doubt, one needs both: to be a circumciser and a slaughterer. And therefore YHWH delivered to Israel two commandments: the blood of Passover and the blood of circumcision, because He wished to save them from the judgment of the configuration and to turn the face of the indication of that star onto slaughter and circumcision — slaughter being the slaughter of the blood of Passover, and circumcision, that is, the blood of circumcision. A hint to the matter: ״רָעָה״ (evil) has the same numerical value as ״עָרְלָה״ (foreskin). And they were commanded concerning both, to be saved from actual killing and from wound and bruise. And Pharaoh said: I see that the star whose name is רָעָה is rising to meet you and to meet all who go up from Egypt, both men, and women and children. If so, how will you correct the two indications of the configuration? The men — well and good — they will correct through the blood of Passover and circumcision, but women and children, how will they correct? For the women are not subject to circumcision, and the children are not in the habit of slaughtering. Therefore, ״לְכוּ נָא הַגְּבָרִים וְעִבְדוּ אֶת ה׳, כִּי אוֹתָהּ אַתֶּם מְבַקְשִׁים״ — to correct the indication of the star, for after all you yourselves already said, ״פֶּן יִפְגָּעֵנוּ בַּדֶּבֶר אוֹ בֶחָרֶב״ (Exodus 5:3). And this is the reason specifically for ״וְנִזְבְּחָה לַה׳ אֱלֹהֵינוּ״ (Exodus 5:3) — not for the going — so that Pharaoh should not say: Go perform some service without slaughter, in order that your livestock remain here. Therefore Moses said ״וְנִזְבְּחָה״, so that those who go would not be stricken by plague or by sword from the aspect of the indication of the star. And therefore he used the language of פְּגִיעָה, striking, which indicates those who go in any case. And if so — your own mouth testifies against you, that you need to correct the face of the indication of the configuration which indicates plague and sword, and this will not be corrected except by means of the men. And of necessity the women and children will remain with us."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:23.133073723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}